WEBVTT

00:00:02.124 --> 00:00:03.952
Take your brother outside
as fast as you can!

00:00:04.190 --> 00:00:05.210
Now, Dean! Go!

00:00:07.051 --> 00:00:07.687
Mary!

00:00:07.859 --> 00:00:08.481
No!

00:00:10.433 --> 00:00:11.452
Dad's on a hunting trip.

00:00:12.684 --> 00:00:14.075
And he hasn't been home in a few days.

00:00:16.145 --> 00:00:17.557
I swore I was done hunting.

00:00:18.249 --> 00:00:19.383
I can't do this alone.

00:00:21.847 --> 00:00:22.788
No!

00:00:25.403 --> 00:00:26.510
We got work to do.

00:00:27.229 --> 00:00:29.613
This was dad's single
most valuable possession.

00:00:29.681 --> 00:00:31.825
Everything he knows about
every evil thing is in here.

00:00:31.963 --> 00:00:33.910
I think he wants us to
pick up where he left off

00:00:33.993 --> 00:00:35.266
You know, saving people,

00:00:35.349 --> 00:00:36.373
Hunting things,

00:00:36.428 --> 00:00:37.342
Family business.

00:00:37.425 --> 00:00:37.840
No.

00:00:37.951 --> 00:00:39.267
I got to find Jessica's killer.

00:00:39.361 --> 00:00:40.785
It's the only thing I can think about.

00:00:40.844 --> 00:00:42.228
Sam, You know we're gonna find dad,

00:00:42.256 --> 00:00:42.662
Right?

00:00:44.468 --> 00:00:45.668
Yeah. I know.

00:01:27.455 --> 00:01:28.248
Nervous flyer?

00:01:29.104 --> 00:01:30.397
It's that obvious, huh?

00:01:31.507 --> 00:01:33.775
You know, what are the odds
of dying in a plane crash?

00:01:33.981 --> 00:01:34.749
I mean, what

00:01:34.918 --> 00:01:35.949
20,000 to one?

00:01:39.809 --> 00:01:40.334
Wow.

00:01:41.084 --> 00:01:42.996
That's, uh, really
reassuring. Thank you.

00:02:08.872 --> 00:02:09.359
Thanks.

00:02:10.146 --> 00:02:10.615
Miranda,

00:02:10.784 --> 00:02:11.421
How are you today?

00:02:11.605 --> 00:02:12.842
I'm doing just fine, Chuck.

00:02:14.454 --> 00:02:15.616
Welcome aboard.

00:02:16.328 --> 00:02:19.083
15c towards the back of
the plane, on the right.

00:02:22.041 --> 00:02:23.259
Have a nice flight, sir.

00:02:26.102 --> 00:02:27.470
Oh, I'm counting on it.

00:02:32.786 --> 00:02:33.442
Um...

00:02:35.241 --> 00:02:36.647
Uh, 11F,

00:02:36.703 --> 00:02:38.615
That's the middle of the
plane, on... Thank you

00:02:40.823 --> 00:02:41.535
...the left.

00:02:53.529 --> 00:02:54.241
Excuse me.

00:02:55.044 --> 00:02:56.319
Do you know how long we've been up?

00:02:56.431 --> 00:02:58.793
Oh, uh... about 40 minutes.

00:02:59.823 --> 00:03:00.386
Wow.

00:03:00.682 --> 00:03:02.050
Time really does fly, huh?

00:03:05.403 --> 00:03:06.115
Excuse me.

00:03:06.190 --> 00:03:07.670
I've got to stretch my legs.

00:03:34.332 --> 00:03:35.661
You, what the hell are you doing?!

00:04:47.793 --> 00:04:48.674
Morning, sunshine.

00:04:50.039 --> 00:04:50.807
What time is it?

00:04:50.957 --> 00:04:52.269
Huh, It's about 5:45.

00:04:52.419 --> 00:04:53.131
In the morning?

00:04:53.206 --> 00:04:53.600
Yep.

00:04:53.806 --> 00:04:54.871
Where does the day go?

00:04:56.933 --> 00:04:58.020
Did you get any sleep last night?

00:04:58.226 --> 00:04:59.575
Yeah, I grabbed a couple hours.

00:04:59.650 --> 00:05:00.288
You, liar

00:05:01.256 --> 00:05:02.381
'Cause I was up at 3:00,

00:05:03.131 --> 00:05:04.930
And you were watching a
George Foreman infomercial.

00:05:05.040 --> 00:05:05.808
Hey, what can I say?

00:05:05.864 --> 00:05:06.745
It's riveting tv.

00:05:07.176 --> 00:05:08.563
When was the last time you
got a good night's sleep?

00:05:08.807 --> 00:05:09.388
I don't know,

00:05:09.463 --> 00:05:11.053
A little while, I guess.
It's not a big deal

00:05:11.241 --> 00:05:11.971
Yeah, it is.

00:05:12.440 --> 00:05:13.864
I appreciate your concern.

00:05:13.902 --> 00:05:15.232
I'm not concerned about you.

00:05:15.251 --> 00:05:17.781
It's your job to keep my ass
alive, so I need you sharp.

00:05:19.198 --> 00:05:20.773
Seriously, are you still
having nightmares about Jess?

00:05:26.264 --> 00:05:26.807
Yeah.

00:05:28.585 --> 00:05:30.272
But it's not just her. It's everything.

00:05:30.703 --> 00:05:32.408
I just forgot, you know? This job.

00:05:33.905 --> 00:05:34.805
Man, it gets to you.

00:05:35.123 --> 00:05:37.129
You can't let it. You can't
bring it home like that.

00:05:38.441 --> 00:05:39.003
So, what?

00:05:39.040 --> 00:05:39.603
All this it...

00:05:39.915 --> 00:05:40.946
Never keeps you up at night?

00:05:42.108 --> 00:05:42.576
Never?

00:05:42.932 --> 00:05:43.645
You're never afraid?

00:05:43.926 --> 00:05:44.807
No, not really.

00:05:53.129 --> 00:05:53.913
That's not fear.

00:05:55.225 --> 00:05:56.125
That is precaution.

00:05:56.706 --> 00:05:57.605
All right, whatever.

00:05:57.643 --> 00:05:58.749
I'm too tired to argue.

00:06:07.703 --> 00:06:08.246
Hello?

00:06:08.525 --> 00:06:08.974
Dean,

00:06:09.237 --> 00:06:10.905
It's Jerry Panowski.

00:06:11.886 --> 00:06:13.901
You and your dad helped
me out a couple years back.

00:06:14.985 --> 00:06:15.937
Oh, all right,

00:06:15.981 --> 00:06:18.771
Yeah, up in kittanning,
Pennsylvania, the poltergeist thing.

00:06:19.213 --> 00:06:20.143
It's not back, is it?

00:06:20.342 --> 00:06:20.807
No.

00:06:21.184 --> 00:06:21.715
No.

00:06:22.955 --> 00:06:23.774
Thank god, no.

00:06:25.254 --> 00:06:27.003
But it's something else, and...

00:06:27.512 --> 00:06:28.862
Well, I think it could be a lot worse.

00:06:29.460 --> 00:06:30.058
What is it?

00:06:30.634 --> 00:06:31.648
Can we talk in person?

00:06:37.427 --> 00:06:39.176
Thanks for making the trip so quick.

00:06:39.281 --> 00:06:41.823
I ought to be doing you guys a
favor, not the other way around.

00:06:42.775 --> 00:06:44.280
Dean and your dad really helped me out.

00:06:44.878 --> 00:06:46.516
Yeah, he told me. It was a poltergeist?

00:06:46.583 --> 00:06:47.225
Poltergeist?

00:06:47.420 --> 00:06:48.328
Man, I loved that movie.

00:06:48.372 --> 00:06:50.232
Hey, nobody's talking
to you. Keep walking.

00:06:51.140 --> 00:06:53.907
Damn right it was a poltergeist
practically tore our house apart.

00:06:54.903 --> 00:06:55.855
Tell you something

00:06:56.493 --> 00:06:57.799
If it wasn't for you and your dad,

00:06:57.910 --> 00:06:59.061
I probably wouldn't be alive.

00:07:01.261 --> 00:07:03.033
Your dad said you were off
at college. Is that right?

00:07:03.652 --> 00:07:04.870
Yeah, I was. I'm...

00:07:05.158 --> 00:07:06.287
Taking some time off.

00:07:06.575 --> 00:07:08.169
Well, he was real proud
of you. I could tell.

00:07:08.612 --> 00:07:09.962
He talked about you all the time.

00:07:11.331 --> 00:07:11.951
He did?

00:07:12.327 --> 00:07:13.323
Yeah, you bet he did.

00:07:13.833 --> 00:07:15.781
Oh, hey, I tried to get
ahold of him, but I couldn't.

00:07:16.334 --> 00:07:17.309
How's he doing, anyway?

00:07:18.460 --> 00:07:19.434
He's, um

00:07:20.023 --> 00:07:21.352
Wrapped up in a job right now.

00:07:21.617 --> 00:07:23.145
Well, we're missing the old man.

00:07:23.411 --> 00:07:24.363
We get sam.

00:07:24.518 --> 00:07:25.691
Even trade, huh?

00:07:26.223 --> 00:07:27.684
No, not by a long shot.

00:07:28.304 --> 00:07:29.964
I got something I want you guys to hear.

00:07:31.823 --> 00:07:32.930
I listened to this.

00:07:33.439 --> 00:07:33.926
Well,

00:07:34.169 --> 00:07:35.653
It sounded like it was up your alley

00:07:35.919 --> 00:07:37.889
Normally I wouldn't have access to this.

00:07:38.040 --> 00:07:41.737
It's the cockpit voice recorder
for united britannia flight 2485.

00:07:42.025 --> 00:07:42.933
It was one of ours.

00:07:43.456 --> 00:07:43.905
Mayday

00:08:06.190 --> 00:08:07.221
Took off from here,

00:08:07.783 --> 00:08:09.555
Crashed about 200 miles south.

00:08:09.834 --> 00:08:11.945
Now, they're saying mechanical failure.

00:08:12.147 --> 00:08:14.490
Cabin depressurized
somehow. Nobody knows why.

00:08:14.848 --> 00:08:16.145
Over 100 people on board.

00:08:16.931 --> 00:08:18.083
Only seven got out alive.

00:08:19.056 --> 00:08:19.837
Pilot was one.

00:08:20.460 --> 00:08:22.380
His name is chuck lambert.
He's a good friend of mine.

00:08:22.962 --> 00:08:23.929
Chuck is, uh...

00:08:25.589 --> 00:08:26.887
Well, he's pretty broken up about it,

00:08:27.708 --> 00:08:28.581
Like it was his fault.

00:08:29.416 --> 00:08:30.223
You don't think it was?

00:08:30.766 --> 00:08:31.614
No, I don't.

00:08:32.334 --> 00:08:32.810
Jerry,

00:08:32.996 --> 00:08:34.836
We're gonna need passenger manifests,

00:08:34.921 --> 00:08:36.390
Hum...a list of survivors.

00:08:36.430 --> 00:08:36.907
All right.

00:08:37.026 --> 00:08:37.661
And huh...

00:08:37.741 --> 00:08:39.277
Any way we can take a
look at the wreckage?

00:08:39.958 --> 00:08:41.190
The other stuff is no problem,

00:08:41.243 --> 00:08:42.064
But the wreckage

00:08:42.850 --> 00:08:45.803
Fellas, the ntsb has it locked
down in an evidence warehouse.

00:08:46.782 --> 00:08:48.292
No way I've got that kind of clearance.

00:08:50.858 --> 00:08:51.348
No problem.

00:08:56.786 --> 00:08:57.237
Hey

00:08:57.395 --> 00:08:57.859
Hi.

00:09:00.825 --> 00:09:01.831
You've been in there forever.

00:09:03.358 --> 00:09:04.391
You can't rush perfection.

00:09:05.132 --> 00:09:06.245
Homeland security?

00:09:07.423 --> 00:09:08.337
That's pretty illegal,

00:09:08.430 --> 00:09:09.118
Even for us.

00:09:09.953 --> 00:09:10.456
Yeah, well,

00:09:10.495 --> 00:09:11.820
It's something new, you know?

00:09:11.833 --> 00:09:13.528
People haven't seen it a thousand times.

00:09:18.337 --> 00:09:19.260
All right, so, what do you got?

00:09:19.479 --> 00:09:20.121
Well,

00:09:20.136 --> 00:09:22.702
There's definitely E.V.P. On
the cockpit voice recorder.

00:09:22.812 --> 00:09:23.156
Yeah?

00:09:23.234 --> 00:09:23.735
Listen.

00:09:31.412 --> 00:09:32.429
"No survivors"?

00:09:33.321 --> 00:09:34.051
What's that supposed to mean?

00:09:34.061 --> 00:09:35.532
There were seven survivors.

00:09:36.122 --> 00:09:36.748
Got me.

00:09:38.996 --> 00:09:40.514
So, what are you
thinking? A haunted flight?

00:09:40.959 --> 00:09:42.587
There's a long history of spirits and

00:09:42.634 --> 00:09:44.638
Death omens on planes and ships,

00:09:44.685 --> 00:09:45.749
Like phantom travelers.

00:09:45.796 --> 00:09:46.203
Mm-Hmm

00:09:46.250 --> 00:09:48.160
Or remember flight 401?

00:09:48.394 --> 00:09:48.848
Right

00:09:49.068 --> 00:09:49.835
The one that crashed,

00:09:49.882 --> 00:09:51.384
The airline salvaged
some of this parts,*

00:09:51.447 --> 00:09:52.527
Put it in other planes,

00:09:52.836 --> 00:09:55.074
Then the spirit of the pilot and
copilot haunted those flights.

00:09:55.137 --> 00:09:55.481
Right.

00:09:55.544 --> 00:09:56.029
Yep.

00:09:56.984 --> 00:09:58.205
Maybe we got a similar deal.

00:09:58.941 --> 00:10:01.320
All rigth so, survivors which
one do you want to talk to first?

00:10:01.373 --> 00:10:03.094
Third on the list Max Jaffey.

00:10:03.188 --> 00:10:03.767
Why him?

00:10:03.814 --> 00:10:05.020
For one, he's from around here.

00:10:05.072 --> 00:10:05.823
And two,

00:10:06.402 --> 00:10:07.780
If anyone saw anything weird.

00:10:08.421 --> 00:10:08.954
He did.

00:10:10.112 --> 00:10:10.973
What makes you say that?

00:10:11.317 --> 00:10:12.554
Well, I spoke to his mother,

00:10:13.359 --> 00:10:14.706
And she told me where to find him.

00:10:17.447 --> 00:10:18.370
I don't understand.

00:10:18.382 --> 00:10:20.329
I already spoke with homeland security.

00:10:20.681 --> 00:10:21.270
Right.

00:10:21.776 --> 00:10:23.308
Some new information has come up.

00:10:23.544 --> 00:10:25.464
So if you could just
answer a couple questions...

00:10:25.669 --> 00:10:27.016
Just before the plane went down,

00:10:27.707 --> 00:10:30.031
Did you notice anything unusual?

00:10:30.368 --> 00:10:31.092
Like what?

00:10:31.884 --> 00:10:33.113
Strange lights,

00:10:33.787 --> 00:10:35.101
Weird noises, maybe...

00:10:35.500 --> 00:10:36.208
Voices.

00:10:38.128 --> 00:10:38.936
No, nothing.

00:10:40.869 --> 00:10:41.711
Mr. Joffey

00:10:42.671 --> 00:10:43.143
Jaffey.

00:10:43.446 --> 00:10:43.951
Jaffey.

00:10:44.086 --> 00:10:45.231
You checked yourself in here,

00:10:45.349 --> 00:10:45.804
Right?

00:10:47.019 --> 00:10:47.815
Can I ask why?

00:10:48.312 --> 00:10:49.619
I was a little stressed.

00:10:49.639 --> 00:10:51.490
I survived a plane crash.

00:10:53.156 --> 00:10:53.733
And that's

00:10:53.833 --> 00:10:54.629
What terrified you?

00:10:54.669 --> 00:10:55.803
That's what you were afraid of?

00:10:55.902 --> 00:10:58.410
I... I don't want to
talk about this anymore.

00:10:58.589 --> 00:11:00.380
I think maybe you did
see something up there.

00:11:01.415 --> 00:11:02.410
We need to know what.

00:11:03.478 --> 00:11:03.956
No.

00:11:04.095 --> 00:11:05.170
No, I was...

00:11:05.309 --> 00:11:06.065
Delusional

00:11:06.844 --> 00:11:07.800
Seeing things.

00:11:09.105 --> 00:11:10.125
He was seeing things.

00:11:13.676 --> 00:11:14.271
It's okay.

00:11:15.737 --> 00:11:18.664
Then just tell us what you
thought you saw, please.

00:11:23.307 --> 00:11:24.038
There was...

00:11:24.277 --> 00:11:24.849
This...

00:11:25.198 --> 00:11:25.866
Man.

00:11:27.551 --> 00:11:28.441
And, uh,

00:11:28.536 --> 00:11:29.951
He had these...

00:11:31.047 --> 00:11:31.670
Eyes...

00:11:31.765 --> 00:11:32.512
These, uh...

00:11:34.587 --> 00:11:35.795
Black eyes.

00:11:37.607 --> 00:11:39.435
And I saw him

00:11:40.215 --> 00:11:42.377
I thought I saw him...

00:11:46.319 --> 00:11:46.923
What?

00:11:49.214 --> 00:11:51.391
He opened the emergency exit.

00:11:53.586 --> 00:11:54.190
But that's...

00:11:54.238 --> 00:11:55.351
That's impossible,

00:11:55.764 --> 00:11:57.022
Right? I mean, I looked it up.

00:11:57.054 --> 00:11:57.944
There's something like

00:11:58.103 --> 00:12:00.200
Two tons of pressure on that door.

00:12:02.364 --> 00:12:02.936
Yeah...

00:12:03.842 --> 00:12:04.732
This man, huh...

00:12:04.812 --> 00:12:07.307
Did he seem to appear and disappear.

00:12:07.564 --> 00:12:09.948
Rapidly.It would look
something like a mirage.

00:12:11.733 --> 00:12:13.052
What are you, nuts?

00:12:15.293 --> 00:12:16.437
He was a passenger.

00:12:16.469 --> 00:12:18.376
He was sitting right in front of me.

00:12:25.485 --> 00:12:26.645
Say here we are

00:12:26.757 --> 00:12:28.902
George Phelps, seat 20c.

00:12:29.538 --> 00:12:30.047
Hmm.

00:12:31.002 --> 00:12:33.196
Man, I don't care how strong you are.

00:12:35.691 --> 00:12:37.725
Even yoked up on pcp or something,

00:12:38.109 --> 00:12:41.097
No way you can open up an
emergency door during a flight.

00:12:42.069 --> 00:12:43.086
Not if you're human.

00:12:44.437 --> 00:12:46.423
But maybe this guy
George was something else

00:12:46.754 --> 00:12:48.915
Some kind of creature,
maybe, in human form.

00:12:49.344 --> 00:12:51.124
Does that look like a
creature's lair to you?

00:12:59.756 --> 00:13:01.059
This is your late husband?

00:13:02.140 --> 00:13:03.523
Yes, that was my george.

00:13:04.344 --> 00:13:05.441
And you said he was a...

00:13:06.299 --> 00:13:07.094
Dentist?

00:13:07.514 --> 00:13:08.097
Mm-Hmm.

00:13:09.374 --> 00:13:11.683
He was headed to a convention in Denver.

00:13:14.547 --> 00:13:16.594
Do you know that he
was petrified to fly?

00:13:20.257 --> 00:13:21.666
For him to go like that...

00:13:24.313 --> 00:13:25.553
How long were you married?

00:13:27.957 --> 00:13:29.159
13 years.

00:13:29.916 --> 00:13:31.118
In all that time,

00:13:32.714 --> 00:13:34.442
Did you ever notice anything...

00:13:34.836 --> 00:13:36.339
Strange about him,

00:13:36.864 --> 00:13:38.479
Anything out of the ordinary?

00:13:41.684 --> 00:13:42.379
Well...

00:13:44.520 --> 00:13:46.682
Uh, he had acid reflux,

00:13:46.813 --> 00:13:47.883
If that's what you mean.

00:13:52.017 --> 00:13:53.202
I mean it goes without saying.

00:13:53.221 --> 00:13:54.635
It just doesn't make any sense.

00:13:55.037 --> 00:13:56.652
A middle-Aged dentist with an ulcer

00:13:56.671 --> 00:13:58.399
Is not exactly evil personified.

00:13:59.169 --> 00:14:01.310
You know what we need to do is
get inside that ntsb warehouse,

00:14:01.328 --> 00:14:02.812
Check out the wreckage.

00:14:04.654 --> 00:14:05.555
Okay.

00:14:05.799 --> 00:14:06.764
But if we're gonna go that route,

00:14:06.793 --> 00:14:07.638
We'd better look the part.

00:14:14.016 --> 00:14:16.253
I look like one of the blues brothers.

00:14:16.572 --> 00:14:17.398
No, you don't.

00:14:17.886 --> 00:14:19.107
You look more like a...

00:14:19.220 --> 00:14:20.854
Seventh-Grader at his first dance.

00:14:23.694 --> 00:14:24.896
I hate this thing.

00:14:24.933 --> 00:14:25.365
Hey.

00:14:25.741 --> 00:14:27.450
You want into that warehouse or not?

00:15:11.444 --> 00:15:12.158
What is that?

00:15:13.322 --> 00:15:14.487
It's an E.M.F. Meter...

00:15:14.937 --> 00:15:16.646
Reads electromagnetic frequencies.

00:15:17.437 --> 00:15:19.291
Yeah, I know what an E.M.F. Meter is,

00:15:19.309 --> 00:15:21.751
But why does that one look
like a busted-Up walkman?

00:15:22.804 --> 00:15:24.006
That's what I made it out of.

00:15:24.757 --> 00:15:25.714
It's homemade.

00:15:27.818 --> 00:15:29.677
Yeah, I can see that.

00:15:56.219 --> 00:15:57.778
Check out emergency door handle.

00:16:03.433 --> 00:16:04.372
What is this stuff?

00:16:04.503 --> 00:16:05.818
One way to find out.

00:16:18.681 --> 00:16:19.864
Homeland security?

00:16:20.697 --> 00:16:21.166
What?

00:16:21.260 --> 00:16:22.706
One team of you guys isn't enough?

00:16:23.345 --> 00:16:24.190
What are you talking about?

00:16:24.380 --> 00:16:26.539
Two of your buddies went
inside not five minutes ago.

00:17:06.927 --> 00:17:08.918
These monkey suits do come in handy.

00:17:10.439 --> 00:17:11.209
Listen Chuck

00:17:11.378 --> 00:17:12.429
It's like getting back on a horse,

00:17:12.977 --> 00:17:14.460
Only in this case, a little twin engine.

00:17:14.779 --> 00:17:15.606
Not even a horse

00:17:15.756 --> 00:17:16.545
More like a pony.

00:17:17.561 --> 00:17:18.481
I'll be right there with you too.

00:17:18.500 --> 00:17:20.490
Anytime you feel like you don't
want the wheel, I'll take over.

00:17:21.411 --> 00:17:22.218
Look, Chuck,

00:17:22.800 --> 00:17:23.927
We don't have to do this today.

00:17:24.303 --> 00:17:25.110
I'm not trying to rush you.

00:17:26.032 --> 00:17:26.746
No, the...

00:17:27.854 --> 00:17:28.849
The waiting is worse.

00:17:31.328 --> 00:17:33.169
Okay, they're filling
up the tank. Then we go.

00:18:06.365 --> 00:18:06.928
Huh.

00:18:08.599 --> 00:18:10.045
This stuff is covered in sulfur.

00:18:10.327 --> 00:18:10.947
You're sure?

00:18:11.660 --> 00:18:12.487
Take a look for yourself.

00:18:12.506 --> 00:18:13.876
"You effin' piece of..."

00:18:13.876 --> 00:18:15.210
If you fellows will excuse me,

00:18:15.247 --> 00:18:16.675
I have an idiot to fire.

00:18:23.603 --> 00:18:23.998
Hmm.

00:18:24.974 --> 00:18:27.754
Here is not too many things that
leave behind a sulfuric residue.

00:18:27.857 --> 00:18:28.833
Demonic possession?

00:18:29.378 --> 00:18:32.495
It would explain how a mortal man would have
the strength to open up an emergency hatch.

00:18:32.666 --> 00:18:34.074
If the guy was possessed,

00:18:34.318 --> 00:18:35.013
It's possible.

00:18:35.316 --> 00:18:37.701
This goes way beyond
floating over a bed or

00:18:37.720 --> 00:18:38.602
Barfing pea soup.

00:18:38.659 --> 00:18:40.180
What mean it's one thing
to possess a person,

00:18:40.217 --> 00:18:42.152
But to use them to take
down an entire airplane?

00:18:42.283 --> 00:18:43.992
You ever heard of
something like this before?

00:18:44.182 --> 00:18:44.707
Never.

00:18:50.623 --> 00:18:51.299
I'm ready.

00:18:51.506 --> 00:18:52.332
Let's do this.

00:19:00.588 --> 00:19:01.395
How you feeling?

00:19:01.658 --> 00:19:02.466
I feel great.

00:19:02.710 --> 00:19:04.531
You'll be back flying
jumbos before you know it.

00:19:04.907 --> 00:19:05.752
I hope so.

00:19:09.472 --> 00:19:10.298
How long we been up?

00:19:10.862 --> 00:19:12.608
Huh... Almost 40 minutes.

00:19:12.965 --> 00:19:13.416
Wow.

00:19:13.773 --> 00:19:14.768
Time really does fly.

00:19:42.049 --> 00:19:42.669
So,

00:19:43.063 --> 00:19:45.166
Every religion in every world culture

00:19:45.223 --> 00:19:48.077
Has the concept of demons
and demonic possession, right?

00:19:48.426 --> 00:19:51.374
I mean christian, native
american, hindu. You name it.

00:19:51.468 --> 00:19:53.140
Yeah, but none of them
describe anything like this.

00:19:53.234 --> 00:19:54.360
Well, that's not exactly true.

00:19:54.398 --> 00:19:55.806
You see according to japanese beliefs,

00:19:55.844 --> 00:19:58.567
Certain demons are
behind certain disasters,

00:19:58.612 --> 00:19:59.476
Both natural

00:19:59.589 --> 00:20:00.453
And man-Made

00:20:00.509 --> 00:20:02.762
One causes earthquakes.
Another causes disease.

00:20:02.781 --> 00:20:04.340
And this one causes plane crashes?

00:20:08.607 --> 00:20:09.771
All right, so, what?

00:20:09.809 --> 00:20:11.837
We have a demonthat's
evolved with the times

00:20:11.875 --> 00:20:13.602
And found a way to
ratchet up the body count?

00:20:14.522 --> 00:20:15.106
Yeah.

00:20:16.252 --> 00:20:16.853
You know,

00:20:17.510 --> 00:20:20.120
Who knows how many planes it's
brought down before this one?

00:20:25.026 --> 00:20:25.533
What?

00:20:27.091 --> 00:20:29.082
I don't know, man. This
isn't our normal gig.

00:20:29.645 --> 00:20:31.298
I mean, demons, they
don't want anything just

00:20:31.373 --> 00:20:33.251
Death and destructionfor its own sake.

00:20:34.246 --> 00:20:34.960
This is big.

00:20:36.389 --> 00:20:37.516
I wish dad was here.

00:20:38.587 --> 00:20:39.845
Yeah. Me too.

00:20:46.609 --> 00:20:46.984
Hello?

00:20:47.360 --> 00:20:48.167
Dean it's Jerry

00:20:48.355 --> 00:20:49.069
Oh, hey, Jerry.

00:20:49.369 --> 00:20:50.327
My pilot friend...

00:20:52.318 --> 00:20:53.444
Chuck Lambert, is dead.

00:20:55.437 --> 00:20:55.925
Wha...

00:20:56.301 --> 00:20:57.446
Jerry, I'm sorry. What happened?

00:20:58.010 --> 00:20:59.850
He and his buddy went
up in a small twin.

00:20:59.925 --> 00:21:00.939
About an hour ago.

00:21:01.578 --> 00:21:02.423
The plane went down.

00:21:02.799 --> 00:21:03.587
Where'd this happen?

00:21:03.907 --> 00:21:06.066
About 60 miles west
of here, near nazareth.

00:21:06.632 --> 00:21:08.078
I'll try to ignore the irony in that.

00:21:08.322 --> 00:21:08.885
I'm sorry?

00:21:09.130 --> 00:21:09.637
Nothing.

00:21:10.369 --> 00:21:12.303
Jerry hang in there, all right?
We'll catch up with you soon.

00:21:14.300 --> 00:21:15.258
Another crash?

00:21:15.465 --> 00:21:15.990
Yeah.

00:21:16.366 --> 00:21:16.836
Let's go.

00:21:17.042 --> 00:21:17.587
Where?

00:21:18.282 --> 00:21:18.901
Nazareth.

00:21:31.210 --> 00:21:31.792
Sulfur?

00:21:34.498 --> 00:21:35.681
Well, that's great.

00:21:36.414 --> 00:21:39.174
All right, that's two plane
crashes involving Chuck Lambert.

00:21:39.850 --> 00:21:41.278
This demon sounds likeit was after him.

00:21:41.684 --> 00:21:42.773
With all due respect to Chuck,

00:21:43.863 --> 00:21:45.966
If that's the case, that
would be the good news.

00:21:46.379 --> 00:21:47.186
What's the bad news?

00:21:47.374 --> 00:21:49.947
Chuck's plane went down
exactly 40 minutes into flight.

00:21:50.112 --> 00:21:50.995
And get this

00:21:51.145 --> 00:21:52.741
So did flight 2485.

00:21:53.042 --> 00:21:53.849
40 minutes?

00:21:54.262 --> 00:21:54.938
What does that mean?

00:21:55.521 --> 00:21:56.835
It's biblical numerology.

00:21:57.098 --> 00:21:59.089
You know Noah's ark,
it rained for 40days.

00:21:59.145 --> 00:22:00.122
The number means death.

00:22:00.518 --> 00:22:01.250
I went back,

00:22:01.325 --> 00:22:03.992
And there have been six plane
crashes over the last decade

00:22:04.030 --> 00:22:06.809
That all went down
exactly 40 minutes in.

00:22:07.861 --> 00:22:08.743
Any survivors?

00:22:09.419 --> 00:22:09.889
No.

00:22:10.331 --> 00:22:10.856
Or not

00:22:10.932 --> 00:22:12.002
Until now,at least

00:22:12.021 --> 00:22:14.312
Not until flight 2485, for some reason.

00:22:15.363 --> 00:22:16.809
And the cockpit voice recorder

00:22:16.922 --> 00:22:18.180
Remember what the E.V.P. Said?

00:22:18.481 --> 00:22:19.345
"No survivors."

00:22:23.331 --> 00:22:24.702
It's going after all the survivors.

00:22:25.922 --> 00:22:27.012
Something finish the job.

00:22:30.920 --> 00:22:31.427
Really?

00:22:32.046 --> 00:22:33.812
Well, thank you for taking our survey,

00:22:33.830 --> 00:22:35.145
And if you do plan to fly,

00:22:35.164 --> 00:22:38.018
Please don't forget your friendsat
united britannia airlines.

00:22:38.751 --> 00:22:39.220
Thanks.

00:22:39.671 --> 00:22:40.309
All right.

00:22:40.424 --> 00:22:43.072
That takes care of Blaines
Anderson and Dennis Holloway.

00:22:43.186 --> 00:22:44.557
They're not flying anytime soon.

00:22:44.614 --> 00:22:47.149
So our only wildcard is the
flight attendant amanda walker.

00:22:47.412 --> 00:22:47.937
Right

00:22:47.975 --> 00:22:50.078
Her sister Karen said her flight
leaves Indianapolis at 8:00.

00:22:50.116 --> 00:22:51.675
Yeah but it's her first
night backon the job.

00:22:51.712 --> 00:22:53.064
That sounds like just our luck.

00:22:53.383 --> 00:22:54.998
Dean, this is a 5-Hour drive made

00:22:55.129 --> 00:22:56.575
Even with you behind the wheel.

00:22:57.159 --> 00:22:58.724
Call amanda's cellphone again,

00:22:58.742 --> 00:23:00.066
See if we can't head
her off at the pass.

00:23:00.121 --> 00:23:01.482
I already left her three voice messages.

00:23:01.500 --> 00:23:03.587
She must have turned her cellphone off.

00:23:04.630 --> 00:23:06.382
God,we're never gonna make it.

00:23:06.438 --> 00:23:07.127
We'll make it.

00:23:21.462 --> 00:23:22.096
Right there.

00:23:22.208 --> 00:23:23.326
They're boarding in 30 minutes.

00:23:23.475 --> 00:23:24.052
Okay.

00:23:24.593 --> 00:23:25.953
We still have some cards to play.

00:23:26.004 --> 00:23:26.992
We need to find a phone.

00:23:30.175 --> 00:23:31.107
Airport Services.

00:23:31.218 --> 00:23:32.299
Hi. Gate 13.

00:23:32.369 --> 00:23:33.524
<i>Who are you calling, Sir</i>

00:23:33.636 --> 00:23:35.253
I'm trying to contact an Amanda Walker.

00:23:35.275 --> 00:23:37.168
She's a flight attendant
on flight, um...

00:23:37.311 --> 00:23:38.588
Flight 424.

00:23:38.720 --> 00:23:39.755
<i>"Amanda walker,"</i>

00:23:40.019 --> 00:23:41.737
<i>"Amanda Walker, you have a phone call"</i>

00:23:41.825 --> 00:23:43.630
<i>"White courtesy phone, gate 13."</i>

00:23:46.569 --> 00:23:47.626
Come on.

00:23:49.233 --> 00:23:50.467
This is amanda walker.

00:23:50.841 --> 00:23:51.611
Miss walker.

00:23:52.052 --> 00:23:53.862
Hi, this is Dr. James Headfield

00:23:53.884 --> 00:23:56.064
From st. Francis memorial hospital.

00:23:56.394 --> 00:23:58.222
We have a Karen Walker here.

00:23:58.420 --> 00:23:59.125
Why Karen?

00:23:59.169 --> 00:24:01.282
Nothing serious just
a minor car accident,

00:24:01.317 --> 00:24:02.836
But she was injured, so

00:24:02.968 --> 00:24:05.962
Wa-Wait, that's impossible. I
just got off the phone with her.

00:24:09.227 --> 00:24:09.844
You what?

00:24:09.932 --> 00:24:10.790
Five minutes ago.

00:24:10.834 --> 00:24:13.499
She's at her house,
cramming for a final.

00:24:13.521 --> 00:24:14.467
Who is this?

00:24:15.668 --> 00:24:16.681
Uh, well...

00:24:17.099 --> 00:24:18.200
There must be some mistake.

00:24:18.222 --> 00:24:20.248
And how would you even know I was here?

00:24:21.987 --> 00:24:23.594
Is this one of Vince's friends?

00:24:25.243 --> 00:24:26.322
Guilty as charged.

00:24:27.136 --> 00:24:29.206
Wow. This is unbelievable.

00:24:30.065 --> 00:24:31.694
He's really sorry.

00:24:32.333 --> 00:24:33.918
Well, you tell him to
mind his own business

00:24:33.962 --> 00:24:35.723
And stay out of my life, okay?

00:24:35.811 --> 00:24:36.733
Yes, but...

00:24:37.085 --> 00:24:38.758
He really needs to see you tonight,

00:24:39.089 --> 00:24:39.815
So

00:24:39.925 --> 00:24:41.401
No, I'm sorry. It's too late.

00:24:41.599 --> 00:24:42.634
Don't be like that.

00:24:43.098 --> 00:24:44.199
Come on. The guy's

00:24:44.354 --> 00:24:45.983
A mess. Really. It's pathetic.

00:24:47.326 --> 00:24:48.009
Really?

00:24:48.229 --> 00:24:48.977
Oh, yeah.

00:24:49.638 --> 00:24:51.157
Look, I've got to go. Um...

00:24:51.168 --> 00:24:53.260
Tell him to call me when I land.

00:24:53.414 --> 00:24:55.176
No, no. Wait, Amanda. Amanda!

00:25:01.892 --> 00:25:02.817
How are you?

00:25:04.226 --> 00:25:05.393
Hey, boss. Hey

00:25:13.370 --> 00:25:14.272
Damn it!

00:25:14.779 --> 00:25:15.858
So close.

00:25:18.368 --> 00:25:20.063
All right, it's time for plan "B."

00:25:20.537 --> 00:25:21.594
We're getting on that plane.

00:25:21.704 --> 00:25:23.377
Oh,oh,Now, just hold on a second.

00:25:23.476 --> 00:25:24.092
Dean,

00:25:24.225 --> 00:25:25.392
That plane is leaving

00:25:25.436 --> 00:25:26.955
With over 100 passengers on board,

00:25:26.977 --> 00:25:27.902
And if we're right,

00:25:28.541 --> 00:25:29.840
That plane is gonna crash.

00:25:29.994 --> 00:25:30.632
I know.

00:25:30.743 --> 00:25:31.315
Okay.

00:25:31.408 --> 00:25:34.094
We're getting on the plane, we need
to find that demon and exorcise it.

00:25:34.138 --> 00:25:36.274
I'll get the tickets. You get
whatever you can out of the trunk.

00:25:36.318 --> 00:25:37.507
Whatever that will make
it through the security.

00:25:37.573 --> 00:25:38.872
Meet me back here in five minutes.

00:25:40.876 --> 00:25:41.889
Are you okay?

00:25:44.256 --> 00:25:45.533
No, not really.

00:25:46.810 --> 00:25:47.955
What? What's wrong?

00:25:50.124 --> 00:25:52.150
Well, I kind of have
this problem with, uh...

00:25:54.285 --> 00:25:55.100
Flying?

00:25:55.519 --> 00:25:57.236
It's never really been
an issue until now.

00:25:57.578 --> 00:25:58.436
You're joking, right?

00:25:58.502 --> 00:25:59.647
Do I look like I'm joking?

00:26:01.431 --> 00:26:03.016
Why do you think I
drive everywhere, sam?

00:26:04.139 --> 00:26:05.923
All right. Uh, I'll go.

00:26:06.212 --> 00:26:06.608
What?

00:26:06.630 --> 00:26:07.665
I'll do this oneon my own.

00:26:08.216 --> 00:26:09.008
Are you, nuts?

00:26:09.559 --> 00:26:10.924
You said that the plane's gonna crash.

00:26:10.968 --> 00:26:12.972
Dean, we can do it together,
or I can do this for myself.

00:26:13.016 --> 00:26:14.887
I'm not seeing a third option, here.

00:26:15.658 --> 00:26:16.583
Come on!

00:26:18.279 --> 00:26:18.962
Really?

00:26:21.274 --> 00:26:22.132
Man...

00:26:35.056 --> 00:26:37.015
Just try to relax. Just try to shut up.

00:27:06.878 --> 00:27:07.847
You're humming Metallica?

00:27:07.869 --> 00:27:09.014
Calms me down.

00:27:11.172 --> 00:27:12.031
Look, man,

00:27:12.405 --> 00:27:13.528
I get you're nervous, all right?

00:27:13.550 --> 00:27:15.113
But you got to stay focused.

00:27:16.452 --> 00:27:16.959
Okay.

00:27:16.981 --> 00:27:17.883
I mean, we got

00:27:17.994 --> 00:27:20.834
32 minutes and counting
to track this thing down

00:27:20.878 --> 00:27:24.159
Or who Everit's possessing, anyway
and perform a full-On exorcism.

00:27:24.181 --> 00:27:26.360
On a crowded plane.That's gonna be easy.

00:27:26.449 --> 00:27:28.078
Take it one step at a time, all right?

00:27:29.792 --> 00:27:30.540
Now,

00:27:30.662 --> 00:27:32.687
Who is it possessing?

00:27:33.766 --> 00:27:35.020
It's usually gonna be somebody

00:27:35.021 --> 00:27:36.078
With some sort of weakness, you know,

00:27:36.100 --> 00:27:38.214
A chink in the armor that
the demon can worm through,

00:27:38.621 --> 00:27:41.395
Somebody with an addiction
or emotional distress.

00:27:43.476 --> 00:27:44.071
Well,

00:27:44.269 --> 00:27:46.030
This is Amanda's first
flight after the crash.

00:27:46.074 --> 00:27:47.682
If I were her, I'd be pretty messed up.

00:27:47.748 --> 00:27:48.452
Mm-Hmm.

00:27:50.324 --> 00:27:51.204
Excuse me.

00:27:51.730 --> 00:27:52.479
Are you Amanda?

00:27:52.633 --> 00:27:53.470
No, I'm not.

00:27:53.514 --> 00:27:55.341
Oh, my mistake.

00:28:01.265 --> 00:28:03.313
All right, well, that's got
to be amanda back there,so

00:28:04.106 --> 00:28:05.162
I'll go talk to her,

00:28:05.295 --> 00:28:07.342
And, uh, I'll get a
read on her mental state.

00:28:07.783 --> 00:28:09.082
What if she's already possessed?

00:28:10.427 --> 00:28:11.880
There's ways to test that.

00:28:14.082 --> 00:28:15.337
I brought holy water.

00:28:16.218 --> 00:28:17.957
No. I think we can go more subtle.

00:28:18.424 --> 00:28:20.604
If she's possessed, she'll
flinch at the name of god.

00:28:21.176 --> 00:28:22.123
Oh. Nice.

00:28:24.259 --> 00:28:24.941
Hey.

00:28:25.107 --> 00:28:25.789
What?

00:28:25.965 --> 00:28:26.846
Say it in latin.

00:28:27.132 --> 00:28:27.793
I know.

00:28:27.881 --> 00:28:28.453
Okay.

00:28:28.696 --> 00:28:29.334
Hey!

00:28:29.841 --> 00:28:30.655
What?!

00:28:30.964 --> 00:28:32.791
Uh, in latin, it's "Cristo."

00:28:32.901 --> 00:28:34.707
Dude, I know! I'm not an idiot!

00:28:47.582 --> 00:28:48.705
Hi. Hi.

00:28:49.762 --> 00:28:50.841
Can I help you with something?

00:28:50.929 --> 00:28:51.832
Oh, no.

00:28:51.876 --> 00:28:53.835
I'm just a bit of an uneasy flier.

00:28:54.200 --> 00:28:55.851
It makes me feel better to
walk around a little bit.

00:28:55.961 --> 00:28:57.899
Oh, it happens to the best of us.

00:28:58.647 --> 00:29:01.686
Of course, you being a stewardess,
I guess flying comes easy to you.

00:29:02.820 --> 00:29:04.009
You'd be surprised.

00:29:04.339 --> 00:29:06.276
Really? You're a nervous flier?

00:29:06.959 --> 00:29:08.610
Yeah, maybe a little bit.

00:29:09.953 --> 00:29:11.605
How is it that,being a stewardess,

00:29:11.946 --> 00:29:13.025
You're scared to fly?

00:29:14.147 --> 00:29:15.381
Kind of a long story.

00:29:16.514 --> 00:29:18.100
Right. I'm sorry for asking.

00:29:18.177 --> 00:29:18.981
It's okay.

00:29:20.335 --> 00:29:21.942
You ever consider other employment?

00:29:23.219 --> 00:29:24.034
No.

00:29:24.562 --> 00:29:26.214
Look, everybody's scared of something.

00:29:26.269 --> 00:29:27.656
I just, uh...

00:29:28.449 --> 00:29:30.408
I'm not gonna let it hold me back.

00:29:31.685 --> 00:29:32.412
Huh.

00:29:33.436 --> 00:29:34.074
So...

00:29:36.893 --> 00:29:37.685
Cristo.

00:29:38.984 --> 00:29:40.305
I'm sorry. Did you say something?

00:29:45.547 --> 00:29:46.405
Cristo?

00:29:47.572 --> 00:29:48.783
I-I didn't, I didn't

00:29:49.818 --> 00:29:51.095
Yeah, nothing. Never mind.

00:29:55.296 --> 00:29:56.155
Okay.

00:30:04.100 --> 00:30:06.962
All right, well, she's got to be the
most well-Adjusted person on the planet.

00:30:07.006 --> 00:30:08.063
You said "cristo"? Yeah.

00:30:08.107 --> 00:30:09.439
And? There's no demon in her.

00:30:09.461 --> 00:30:11.024
There's no demon getting in her.

00:30:11.090 --> 00:30:12.874
So, if it's on the
plane, it can be anyone...

00:30:13.006 --> 00:30:14.063
Anywhere.

00:30:14.856 --> 00:30:17.035
Come on! That can't be normal! Hey, hey,

00:30:17.113 --> 00:30:19.447
It's just a little turbulence.

00:30:19.777 --> 00:30:21.340
Sam, this plane is going to crash, okay?

00:30:21.385 --> 00:30:22.838
So quit treating me
like I'm friggin' fool.

00:30:22.926 --> 00:30:24.709
You need to calm down.
No, I'm sorry I can't.

00:30:24.753 --> 00:30:26.063
Yes, you can.

00:30:26.459 --> 00:30:29.388
Dude, Stow the touchy-Feely,
self-Help yoga crap.

00:30:29.432 --> 00:30:30.489
It's not helping. Listen,
if you're panicked,

00:30:30.533 --> 00:30:31.744
You're wide opento demonic possession,

00:30:31.766 --> 00:30:33.836
So you need to calm yourself down

00:30:33.946 --> 00:30:34.936
Right now.

00:30:43.901 --> 00:30:44.694
Good.

00:30:45.971 --> 00:30:46.719
Now,

00:30:47.325 --> 00:30:49.659
I found an exorcism in here
that I think is gonna work

00:30:50.254 --> 00:30:51.487
The ritual romano.

00:30:52.544 --> 00:30:53.424
What do we have to do?

00:30:53.887 --> 00:30:54.680
It's two parts.

00:30:54.724 --> 00:30:57.146
The first part expels the
demon from the victim's body.

00:30:57.301 --> 00:31:00.405
It makes it manifest, which
actually makes it more powerful.

00:31:00.680 --> 00:31:01.451
More powerful?

00:31:01.561 --> 00:31:02.463
Yeah. How?

00:31:03.146 --> 00:31:04.599
Well, it doesn't need to
possess someone anymore.

00:31:04.643 --> 00:31:06.471
It can just wreak havoc on its own.

00:31:06.735 --> 00:31:08.298
Oh. And why is that a good thing?

00:31:08.827 --> 00:31:10.808
Well, because the second part

00:31:11.689 --> 00:31:13.164
Sends the bastard back to hell

00:31:13.561 --> 00:31:14.728
Once and for all.

00:31:16.247 --> 00:31:17.942
First thing's first we got to find it.

00:31:55.491 --> 00:31:56.423
Ohh! Don't do that.

00:31:56.531 --> 00:31:57.333
Anything?

00:31:57.527 --> 00:31:59.390
No, nothing. How much time we got?

00:31:59.650 --> 00:32:00.538
15 minutes.

00:32:01.795 --> 00:32:03.116
Maybe we missed somebody.

00:32:03.874 --> 00:32:05.390
Maybe the thing's just not on the plane.

00:32:06.660 --> 00:32:07.613
You believe that?

00:32:08.371 --> 00:32:09.454
Well, I will if you will.

00:32:18.958 --> 00:32:19.933
What? What is it?

00:32:21.255 --> 00:32:21.969
Cristo.

00:32:37.116 --> 00:32:38.286
She's not gonna believe this.

00:32:38.437 --> 00:32:39.476
12 minutes, dude.

00:32:41.890 --> 00:32:42.735
Oh, hi.

00:32:43.491 --> 00:32:45.084
Flight's not too bumpy for you, I hope.

00:32:45.157 --> 00:32:47.330
Actually, that's kind of what
we need to talk to you about.

00:32:47.547 --> 00:32:49.430
Um, okay.What can I do for you?

00:32:49.913 --> 00:32:51.507
This is gonna sound nuts, but

00:32:51.871 --> 00:32:54.165
We just don't have time for the whole
"the true this out there" speech right now.

00:32:54.213 --> 00:32:56.362
Look, we know you were on flight 2485.

00:32:58.098 --> 00:32:59.040
Who are you guys?

00:32:59.160 --> 00:33:01.309
Now, we've spoken to
some other survivors.

00:33:01.430 --> 00:33:03.820
We know something brought down that
plane and it wasn't a mechanical failure.

00:33:03.893 --> 00:33:04.907
We need your help

00:33:04.979 --> 00:33:06.694
Because we need to stop
from happening again.

00:33:06.814 --> 00:33:07.716
Here. Now. I'm sorry

00:33:07.788 --> 00:33:10.638
Here. I-I'm very busy. Whoa,
whoa, whoa, whoa. Wait a second.

00:33:10.710 --> 00:33:12.110
I'm not gonna hurt you, okay?

00:33:12.255 --> 00:33:13.631
But listen to me, huh...

00:33:13.752 --> 00:33:16.039
The pilot in 2485, Chuck Lambert.

00:33:16.160 --> 00:33:17.029
He's dead.

00:33:17.712 --> 00:33:18.750
Wait. What?

00:33:18.919 --> 00:33:20.126
What, Chuck is dead?

00:33:20.416 --> 00:33:21.961
He died in a plane crash.

00:33:22.106 --> 00:33:23.652
That's two plane crashes in two months.

00:33:23.676 --> 00:33:25.318
That doesn't strike you as strange?

00:33:26.066 --> 00:33:27.853
Look, there was
something wrong with 2485.

00:33:27.878 --> 00:33:29.203
Now maybe you're
sensitive maybe you didn't

00:33:29.228 --> 00:33:30.628
But there's something
wrong with this flight, too.

00:33:30.653 --> 00:33:32.303
Amanda,you have to believe us.

00:33:37.609 --> 00:33:38.534
On...

00:33:39.484 --> 00:33:41.209
On 2485,

00:33:41.259 --> 00:33:43.059
There was this man.

00:33:43.109 --> 00:33:45.234
He...had these eyes.

00:33:45.509 --> 00:33:47.162
Yes. That's exactly
what we're talking about.

00:33:47.184 --> 00:33:48.837
I don't understand what
are you asking me to do?

00:33:48.859 --> 00:33:50.648
Okay. The copilot, we need
you bring him back here.

00:33:50.693 --> 00:33:52.754
Why? What does he have
to do with anything?

00:33:52.821 --> 00:33:53.750
Don't have time to explain.

00:33:53.772 --> 00:33:55.199
We just need to talk to him. Okay?

00:33:55.312 --> 00:33:56.693
How am I supposed to go in the cockpit

00:33:56.738 --> 00:33:58.572
And get the copilot--
Do whatever it takes

00:33:58.617 --> 00:34:00.293
Tell him there's
something broken back here,

00:34:00.338 --> 00:34:01.719
Whatever will get him
out of that cockpit.

00:34:01.787 --> 00:34:03.213
Do you know that I could lose my job

00:34:03.236 --> 00:34:05.410
If you -- You're gonna lose a
lot more if you don't help us out.

00:34:12.008 --> 00:34:12.755
Okay.

00:34:52.834 --> 00:34:53.989
Yeah, what's the problem?

00:35:00.170 --> 00:35:02.841
Wait. What are you doing? You said
you were just gonna talk to him.

00:35:02.887 --> 00:35:04.358
We are gonna talk to him.

00:35:13.397 --> 00:35:14.718
Oh, my god.What's wrong with him?

00:35:14.784 --> 00:35:15.709
Look. We need you calm.

00:35:15.753 --> 00:35:17.537
We need you outside the curtain.
Well, I don't underst..., I don't know

00:35:17.581 --> 00:35:19.166
Don't let anybody in,
okay? Can you do that?

00:35:19.210 --> 00:35:20.487
Can you do that?

00:35:20.795 --> 00:35:21.380
Amanda?

00:35:21.623 --> 00:35:22.177
Okay.

00:35:22.907 --> 00:35:23.483
Okay.

00:35:25.161 --> 00:35:27.331
Hurry up, sam. I don't know
how much longer I can hold him.

00:35:49.248 --> 00:35:50.842
I know what happened to your girlfriend!

00:35:52.768 --> 00:35:54.318
She must have died screaming!

00:35:55.004 --> 00:35:56.642
Even now, she's burning!

00:35:59.551 --> 00:36:00.260
Sam!

00:36:03.865 --> 00:36:05.038
"Prayer"...

00:36:07.761 --> 00:36:08.470
I got him.

00:36:29.398 --> 00:36:30.018
Where'd he go?

00:36:30.085 --> 00:36:30.992
He's in the plane.

00:36:31.059 --> 00:36:32.564
Hurry up.We got to finish it.

00:38:19.895 --> 00:38:20.426
I don't know.

00:38:20.515 --> 00:38:21.733
I was walking through the airport,

00:38:21.976 --> 00:38:23.283
Then it all goes blank.

00:38:23.570 --> 00:38:25.740
I don't even remember
getting on the plane.

00:38:27.751 --> 00:38:28.902
Anything else?

00:38:29.279 --> 00:38:30.186
No, that's all.

00:38:33.968 --> 00:38:34.920
"Thank you"

00:38:41.318 --> 00:38:42.337
Let's get out of here.

00:38:45.281 --> 00:38:46.123
You okay?

00:38:47.827 --> 00:38:48.580
Dean,

00:38:50.550 --> 00:38:52.166
It knew about Jessica.

00:38:54.841 --> 00:38:57.210
Sam, these things,t-They read minds.

00:38:57.586 --> 00:38:58.317
They lie.

00:38:59.091 --> 00:39:00.309
All right?That's all it was.

00:39:01.992 --> 00:39:02.612
Yeah.

00:39:05.054 --> 00:39:05.829
Come on.

00:39:12.028 --> 00:39:14.370
Nobody knows what you
guys did, but i do.

00:39:15.787 --> 00:39:17.470
A lot of people could have been killed.

00:39:18.931 --> 00:39:20.277
Your dad's gonna be real proud.

00:39:20.808 --> 00:39:22.137
We'll see you around, Jerry.

00:39:25.369 --> 00:39:26.344
You know, Jerry.

00:39:26.676 --> 00:39:27.251
Yeah.

00:39:27.867 --> 00:39:30.480
I meant to ask you how did you
get my cellphone number, anyway?

00:39:30.524 --> 00:39:32.162
I've only had it for like six months.

00:39:32.428 --> 00:39:33.624
Your dad gave it to me.

00:39:34.266 --> 00:39:34.704
What?

00:39:34.749 --> 00:39:36.077
When did you talk to him?

00:39:36.254 --> 00:39:38.690
I mean, I didn't exactly talk to him,but

00:39:39.110 --> 00:39:41.767
I called his number. His voice
message said to give you a call.

00:39:43.711 --> 00:39:44.508
Thanks again, guys.

00:40:01.400 --> 00:40:02.884
This doesn't make any sense, man.

00:40:02.906 --> 00:40:05.054
I've called dad's number like 50 times.

00:40:05.077 --> 00:40:06.383
It's been out of service.

00:40:07.706 --> 00:40:08.902
This is John Winchester.

00:40:09.234 --> 00:40:10.540
I can't be reached.

00:40:10.549 --> 00:40:12.896
If this is an emergency,
call my son, Dean

00:40:13.848 --> 00:40:18.648

866-907-3235

00:40:19.644 --> 00:40:20.729
He'll can help.



00:00:0.500 --> 00:00:2.00
